# Obsidian local plugin state
data.json
# data.json holds API keys, and hand-made copies of it are not covered by the
# bare name above or by *.bak — `data.json.bak-20260810-175409` matches neither
# and sat untracked in the working tree, one `git add -A` away from publishing
# those keys.
data.json.bak*
data.json.*.bak
data.json.orig

# Local backups and generated bundles
backup-*/
*.bak
# Same footgun as the data.json case above, generalized: this repo
# names backups <file>.bak-<timestamp>-<description>, which *.bak alone
# does not match (no trailing ".bak"). Catch that shape too.
*.bak-*
*.map

# Local/editor files
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.agents/
.playwright-cli/
output/
deduction-debug.log
snapshot-source-build-*/
*.bundle

# A plugin checkout must never acquire a Vault-style Research tree. A prior
# test run created this path under the plugin root; keeping the exact root
# ignored prevents it from entering a release without hiding fixture folders
# named Research elsewhere in the repository.
/Research/
agent-canvas-demo/node_modules/
agent-canvas-demo/.git-history/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
agent-canvas-demo/bridge/bridge.config.json
agent-canvas-demo/bridge/.env
agent-canvas-demo/bridge/*.log
agent-canvas-demo/bridge/*.pid
agent-canvas-demo/bridge/audit/
agent-canvas-demo/bridge/runtime/

# Local institutional-login cookies / private runtime state
Scholarium/secrets/
**/Scholarium/secrets/
Scholarium/runtime/
**/Scholarium/runtime/
*.cookies.txt
webvpn-cookies.txt
